{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["The heh <b>shafkhah.</b> In place of the plural form, like שָׁפְכָה in Ashurite script. And by way of derash it reverts to singular, for 'hand' (יד) is grammatically feminine in the majority." "<b>and our eyes did not see.</b> And it is possible that HaShem commanded the nearby city to do this, for had they not committed a transgression like it, it would not have befallen them that a person near them would be killed. And the thoughts of HaShem are deep and exalted beyond measure to us:" "<b>and they shall answer and say.</b> Like וְעָנִיתָ וְאָמַרְתָּ (and you shall answer and say), and there I will explain it:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "Reading 'Ashurite script' for אשורי, i.e., the square/Assyrian letterforms; the point appears to concern orthography or script tradition of the consonantal text."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:10.883176388Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}